\ Spitfire: the scenery that stays put. The coasts, lochs and rivers come
\ from geography.telic; the hills are the real summits it names, with ridges
\ of lesser tops either side of them laid along the ranges' directions (the
\ Pentlands south-west to north-east, the Ochils and Campsies west to east)
\ and Highland hills along both sides of Loch Ness, whose heights are
\ representative rather than surveyed. The towns are their landmarks at the
\ map's positions, built to their published heights where a figure exists
\ (the Forth Bridge's towers 110 m above high water and its rail 46 m, the
\ Scott Monument 61 m, the University's tower 85 m), with streets of
\ tenements, shops and New Town terraces between them; the airfields are the
\ RAF stations of 1940: Turnhouse and Drem for Edinburgh, Abbotsinch for
\ Glasgow, Dalcross for Inverness. Everything is built once into objects and
\ gathered into the collection the view culls.

0xb8c8e0 constant coast-colour
0x6a9ad0 constant bank-colour
0x7c9a5a constant hill-colour
0xc8c0b0 constant stone-colour
0xa09080 constant town-colour
0xd04030 constant bridge-colour
0xe8e8e0 constant runway-colour
0x90a070 constant field-colour
0x5a8040 constant tree-colour

variable scenery
[ ] to scenery
\ every hill as [ x z radius height ], for the ground's height under the aircraft
variable hill-cones
[ ] to hill-cones

\ the ground's height at a point: the tallest hill's cone over it, else sea level
: ground-height ( x z -- height )
	| x z |
	hill-cones 0 ( highest cone |
		cone spread to peak to reach to cone-z to cone-x
		cone-x x - sq cone-z z - sq + sqrt reach / 1 swap - peak * highest max2
	) reduce ;

\ the water's rings, gathered as the scenery is built: the map's frame, the land's outlines, the lochs, the islands and the rivers' strips across the land
variable water-rings
[ ] to water-rings

\ add a ring to the water's
: keep-water-ring ( ring -- )
	| ring ^water-rings |
	water-rings ring add-last! drop ;

\ add a finished sketch to the scenery
: keep ( sketch colour -- )
	| sketch colour ^scenery |
	scenery sketch colour sketch>object add-last! drop ;

\ a landmark's ground point, [ x 0 z ]
: landmark-ground ( key -- point )
	| key |
	landmarks key @ spread drop to z to x
	[ x 0 z ] ;

\ a landmark's height from the map
: landmark-height ( key -- metres ) landmarks swap @ 2 @i ;

\ the heading from one landmark to another, degrees
: landmark-heading ( from to -- degrees )
	| origin destination |
	destination landmark-ground origin landmark-ground v- heading-of ;

\ === lines on the ground ===

\ a path as objects of at most twelve points each, so each piece culls on its own
: keep-path ( points colour -- )
	| points colour |
	0 points size 1- 11 do start
		points start skip 12 take to piece
		piece size 2 >= if
			new-sketch to sketch
			sketch piece sketch-path
			sketch colour keep
		then
	loop ;

\ a closed shore as a path back to its start
: keep-shore ( points colour -- )
	| points colour |
	points [ points first ] concat colour keep-path ;

\ a stretch of river as a ring of [ x z ] points: one bank downstream, the other back up
: river-ring ( course half-width -- ring )
	| course half-width |
	course half-width offset-path course half-width negate offset-path reverse concat
	( point | [ point first point 2 @i ] ) map ;

\ a river as its two banks either side of its course, and its strips of water where its course crosses land: runs of the segments whose middles are not already water
: keep-river ( course half-width -- )
	| course half-width |
	course half-width offset-path bank-colour keep-path
	course half-width negate offset-path bank-colour keep-path
	[ ] to run
	0 course size 1- 1 do k
		course k @i to start
		course k 1+ @i to finish
		start first finish first + 2 / start second finish second + 2 / water-at? if
			run size 2 >= if run half-width river-ring keep-water-ring then
			[ ] to run
		else
			run size 0 = if run start add-last! drop then
			run finish add-last! drop
		then
	loop
	run size 2 >= if run half-width river-ring keep-water-ring then ;

\ an island too small for the map's land: a ring of eight points round its landmark, as land amid the water
: keep-island ( key radius -- )
	| key radius |
	key landmark-ground to centre
	[ 0 8 1 do k
		k 8 / TAU * to angle
		[ centre first angle sin radius * + centre 2 @i angle cos radius * + ]
	loop ] keep-water-ring ;

: build-waters ( -- )
	| ^water-rings |
	land-outlines [ south-land ] concat to water-rings
	lochs values ( loch | loch@shores ( shore | shore keep-water-ring ) each ) each
	water-rings water-rings!
	coastlines ( coast | coast 0 ground-path coast-colour keep-path ) each
	lochs values ( loch |
		loch@shores ( shore | shore loch@height ground-path bank-colour keep-shore ) each
	) each
	rivers@clyde 90 keep-river
	rivers@forth 70 keep-river
	rivers@kelvin 12 keep-river
	rivers@ness ( course | course 25 keep-river ) each
	[ [ :inchkeith 500 ] [ :inchcolm 300 ] [ :cramond-island 300 ] [ :bass-rock 200 ] ] ( island | island spread keep-island ) each
	norway-shores ( shore | shore 0 ground-path coast-colour keep-path ) each
	:faettenfjord landmark-ground to norway-centre
	[ [ 0 130000 water-rings rings>edge-set ]
	  [ norway-centre first norway-centre 2 @i norway-outlines norway-bands concat rings>edge-set ] ] water-regions!
	[ 0 0 0 ] use-water-near ;

\ === hills ===

\ a cone of ground for the ground's height alone, where a model draws the hill itself
: keep-cone ( centre radius height -- )
	| centre radius height ^hill-cones |
	hill-cones [ centre first centre 2 @i radius height ] add-last! drop ;

\ a hill at a point
: keep-hill ( centre radius height seed -- )
	| centre radius height seed |
	centre radius height keep-cone
	new-sketch to sketch
	sketch centre radius height seed sketch-hill
	sketch hill-colour keep ;

\ a range: its highest summit at a point and lesser tops either side along a heading, a spacing apart
: keep-range ( centre heading spacing heights radius -- )
	| centre heading spacing heights radius |
	heights 0 ' max2 reduce to highest
	heights highest position-of to peak-index
	0 heights size 1 do k
		centre heading 0 0 k peak-index - spacing * placed radius heights k @i k 1.7 * keep-hill
	loop ;

: build-hills ( -- )
	:arthurs-seat landmark-ground 700 :arthurs-seat landmark-height 1 keep-hill
	:calton-hill landmark-ground 250 :calton-hill landmark-height 2 keep-hill
	:st-margarets-chapel landmark-ground 160 78 keep-cone
	:scald-law landmark-ground 40 2800 [ 420 510 :scald-law landmark-height 520 480 ] 1500 keep-range
	:ben-cleuch landmark-ground 75 3200 [ 520 610 :ben-cleuch landmark-height 650 580 500 ] 1700 keep-range
	:west-lomond landmark-ground 1600 :west-lomond landmark-height 4 keep-hill
	:earls-seat landmark-ground 80 2600 [ 480 :earls-seat landmark-height 540 500 ] 1500 keep-range
	:ben-lomond landmark-ground 2600 :ben-lomond landmark-height 5 keep-hill
	:tinto landmark-ground 2200 :tinto landmark-height 6 keep-hill
	:north-berwick-law landmark-ground 400 :north-berwick-law landmark-height 7 keep-hill
	:bass-rock landmark-ground 200 :bass-rock landmark-height 8 keep-hill
	:craig-phadrig landmark-ground 600 172 9 keep-hill
	:inchkeith landmark-ground 500 60 10 keep-hill
	:inchcolm landmark-ground 300 30 11 keep-hill
	:cramond-island landmark-ground 300 :cramond-island landmark-height 12 keep-hill
	:stirling-castle landmark-ground 300 75 13 keep-hill
	:wallace-monument landmark-ground 400 90 14 keep-hill
	:dumbarton-castle landmark-ground 200 73 15 keep-hill
	\ the Highland hills either side of Loch Ness, along the Great Glen
	:urquhart-castle landmark-ground to glen-centre
	-20000 20001 4000 do along
		[ -1 1 ] ( side |
			glen-centre 40 side 4500 * 0 along placed
			2200 along side + 0.37 * sin 150 * 600 + 20 along 1000 / + side + keep-hill
		) each
	loop ;

\ === airfields ===

\ an RAF airfield of 1940: the landing ground's boundary, a runway with dashes down it, hangars and the watch office, beside a point on a heading
: keep-airfield ( centre heading -- )
	| centre heading |
	new-sketch to field
	field centre heading 1600 1600 0 rectangle-corners sketch-loop
	field field-colour keep
	new-sketch to runway
	runway centre heading 46 1250 0 rectangle-corners sketch-loop
	-560 561 80 do along
		runway [ centre heading 0 0 along placed centre heading 0 0 along 40 + placed ] sketch-path
	loop
	runway runway-colour keep
	new-sketch to hangars
	[ -260 -130 0 ] ( along | hangars centre heading 520 0 along placed heading 40 60 12 15 sketch-house ) each
	hangars centre heading 470 0 160 placed heading 14 10 8 sketch-box
	hangars centre heading 470 0 230 placed 0 3 3 10 sketch-box
	hangars town-colour keep ;

: build-airfields ( -- )
	:turnhouse landmark-ground 60 keep-airfield
	:drem landmark-ground 90 keep-airfield
	:abbotsinch landmark-ground 50 keep-airfield
	:dalcross landmark-ground 60 keep-airfield
	:wick landmark-ground 130 keep-airfield ;

\ === streets ===

\ whether any of a block's ends or its middle stands on water
: block-in-water? ( start heading across along length -- flag )
	| start heading across along length |
	[ length -2 / 0 length 2 / ] ( offset |
		start heading across 0 along offset + placed to point
		point first point 2 @i water-at?
	) any? ;

\ a row of tenements along a street: blocks a length long and a height high, either side or one side, leaving out any block that would stand in water
: keep-street ( start heading n-blocks length gap height sides -- )
	| start heading n-blocks length gap height sides |
	new-sketch to street
	0 n-blocks 1 do k
		k length gap + * length 2 / + to along
		sides ( side |
			start heading side 22 * along length block-in-water? not if
				street start heading side 22 * 0 along placed heading 14 length height sketch-box
			then
		) each
	loop
	street@points size 0 > if street town-colour keep then ;

\ === the Forth Bridge ===

\ one double cantilever: a tower 110 m high on its pier and an arm reaching each way to its tip at the rail, its sides leaning in from 18 m apart at the water to 5 m at the top
: keep-cantilever ( origin heading along -- )
	| origin heading along |
	new-sketch to cantilever
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ -1 1 ] ( way |
			origin heading side 18 * 0 along way 40 * + placed to foot
			origin heading side 5 * 110 along way 22 * + placed to tower-top
			origin heading side 8 * 46 along way 247 * + placed to tip
			origin heading side 14 * 26 along way 150 * + placed to bow
			cantilever [ foot tower-top tip bow foot ] sketch-path
			cantilever [ bow foot tower-top bow ] sketch-path
			foot tower-top 0.5 v-between to tower-middle
			cantilever [ tower-middle bow tower-top tip 0.5 v-between bow ] sketch-path
		) each
		cantilever [ origin heading side 18 * 0 along 40 - placed origin heading side 18 * 0 along 40 + placed ] sketch-path
		cantilever [ origin heading side 5 * 110 along 22 - placed origin heading side 5 * 110 along 22 + placed ] sketch-path
	) each
	[ -22 22 ] ( at | cantilever [ origin heading -5 110 along at + placed origin heading 5 110 along at + placed ] sketch-path ) each
	cantilever bridge-colour keep ;

: build-forth-bridge ( -- )
	:inchgarvie :north-queensferry landmark-heading to bridge-heading
	:inchgarvie landmark-ground to bridge-centre
	[ -600 0 600 ] ( along | bridge-centre bridge-heading along keep-cantilever ) each
	new-sketch to deck
	[ -6 6 ] ( side |
		deck [ bridge-centre bridge-heading side 46 -1437 placed bridge-centre bridge-heading side 46 1030 placed ] sketch-path
	) each
	[ -353 353 ] ( middle |
		[ -6 6 ] ( side |
			deck [ bridge-centre bridge-heading side 46 middle 53 - placed bridge-centre bridge-heading side 60 middle placed
			       bridge-centre bridge-heading side 46 middle 53 + placed ] sketch-path
		) each
	) each
	-1437 -846 50 do along
		deck [ bridge-centre bridge-heading 0 0 along placed bridge-centre bridge-heading 0 46 along placed ] sketch-path
	loop
	847 1031 50 do along
		deck [ bridge-centre bridge-heading 0 0 along placed bridge-centre bridge-heading 0 46 along placed ] sketch-path
	loop
	deck bridge-colour keep ;

\ === shipyards ===

\ a shipyard crane: a tower and its hammerhead jib
: sketch-crane ( sketch foot heading -- )
	| sketch foot heading |
	sketch foot heading 8 8 46 sketch-box
	sketch [ foot heading 0 46 -25 placed foot heading 0 46 45 placed foot heading 0 52 0 placed foot heading 0 46 -25 placed ] sketch-path ;

\ a ship's hull on a slipway: its deck outline and keel line
: sketch-hull ( sketch centre heading length -- )
	| sketch centre heading length |
	length 2 / to half
	sketch [ centre heading 0 0 half negate placed centre heading -11 12 half negate 20 + placed centre heading -11 12 half placed
	         centre heading 0 14 half 15 + placed centre heading 11 12 half placed centre heading 11 12 half negate 20 + placed ] sketch-loop
	sketch [ centre heading 0 0 half negate placed centre heading 0 0 half placed centre heading 0 14 half 15 + placed ] sketch-path ;

\ === Stirling and Urquhart ===

: build-stirling ( -- )
	:stirling-castle landmark-ground [ 0 75 0 ] v+ to castle-top
	new-sketch to stirling
	stirling castle-top 70 50 80 14 20 sketch-house
	stirling castle-top 70 60 0 0 placed 70 40 50 14 sketch-box
	stirling stone-colour keep
	new-sketch to monument
	monument :wallace-monument landmark-ground [ 0 90 0 ] v+ 10 55 12 sketch-spire
	monument stone-colour keep ;

: build-urquhart ( -- )
	new-sketch to urquhart
	urquhart :urquhart-castle landmark-ground [ 0 16 0 ] v+ 0 12 12 22 sketch-box
	urquhart :urquhart-castle landmark-ground [ 0 16 0 ] v+ 70 60 0 0 placed 70 40 30 6 sketch-box
	urquhart stone-colour keep ;

\ === the cruisers in the Forth ===

\ a cruiser at anchor: the hull's outline at the waterline and the deck, the bridge and superstructure, two funnels, four turrets
: keep-cruiser ( centre heading -- )
	| centre heading |
	new-sketch to ship
	ship [ centre heading 0 0 -90 placed centre heading -10 0 -70 placed centre heading -10 0 75 placed centre heading 0 0 95 placed
	       centre heading 10 0 75 placed centre heading 10 0 -70 placed ] sketch-loop
	ship [ centre heading 0 8 -90 placed centre heading -10 8 -70 placed centre heading -10 8 75 placed centre heading 0 9 95 placed
	       centre heading 10 8 75 placed centre heading 10 8 -70 placed ] sketch-loop
	ship centre heading 0 8 15 placed heading 12 30 10 sketch-box
	ship centre heading 0 18 25 placed heading 8 10 12 sketch-box
	[ -5 12 ] ( along | ship centre heading 0 18 along placed 0 5 5 12 sketch-box ) each
	[ -60 -45 45 60 ] ( along | ship centre heading 0 8 along placed heading 7 8 4 sketch-box ) each
	ship stone-colour keep ;

: build-ships ( -- )
	:inchgarvie :north-queensferry landmark-heading to bridge-heading
	:inchgarvie landmark-ground bridge-heading 90 + 0 0 1800 placed bridge-heading 60 + keep-cruiser
	:inchgarvie landmark-ground bridge-heading 90 + 300 0 2300 placed bridge-heading 70 + keep-cruiser ;
